# Local test and remote-machine configuration template.
# Copy to `.env` (which is gitignored) and uncomment only what you need.
#
# Rules:
# - NEVER commit `.env`, and NEVER store raw passwords or SSH private keys here
#   (keep keys in ~/.ssh/ or a chmod 600 config outside the repository).
# - Explicit environment variables / CLI flags always override `.env`.
# - Standard unit tests (`make test`) never read `.env`.
# - Set DOTENV_DISABLE=1 to ignore `.env` for a single command.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Remote Linux physical host (KVM / GPU / native Linux test runner)
# Used by `make test-remote` and `e2e/machines/machines.py remote - ...`.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SSH host alias from ~/.ssh/config (or user@host):
# LINUX_TEST_HOST=linux-kvm
# Optional extra SSH arguments (e.g. a dedicated config outside the repo):
# LINUX_TEST_SSH_OPTS="-F ~/.config/test-hosts/ssh.config"

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Multi-kernel / VM matrix (`e2e/machines/machines.py`)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MACHINES_WORK=/tmp/machines-work
# MACHINES_CACHE=/tmp/machines-cache
# MACHINES_SSH_OPTS="-F ~/.config/test-hosts/ssh.config"
# MACHINES_ARCH=arm64
# MACHINES_EMULATE=0
# MACHINES_TTL=7200

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Disposable Windows VMs / remote Windows host (`make test-win` / `winvm.py`)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Remote Windows SSH host alias (e.g. Proxmox/lab Windows VM):
# WIN_TEST_HOST=win-lab
# WINVM_SSH_OPTS="-F ~/.config/test-hosts/ssh.config"
# Local golden Windows qcow2/vhdx base image (booted via macOS HVF or Linux KVM CoW overlay):
# WINVM_BASE=~/.cache/win-vm/windows-base.qcow2
# WINVM_WORK=/tmp/winvm-work
# WINVM_DOCKUR_IMAGE=dockurr/windows:latest
# WINVM_TTL=7200

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Integration, E2E & Linux container tests (`make it`, `make e2e`, `make test-linux`)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HC_TEST_BIN=/path/to/herdr-core
# E2E_CODE_SERVER_SEED=/path/to/code-server-seed
# IT_WITH_VSCODE=1
# E2E_REQUIRE_DOCKER=1
# LINUX_TEST_ALL=1

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local CI (`make ci-local` via nektos/act)
# Note: `scripts/ci-local.sh` passes `--env-file /dev/null` to `act` by default
# so host paths in `.env` do not leak into CI containers.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ACT_ARCH=linux/arm64
# ACT_BASE_IMAGE=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-24.04
# ACT_ARTIFACTS_DIR=dist/act-artifacts
# ACT_ENV_FILE=/dev/null
